For $n=2p+1$, put $$u_l=\operatorname{arsinh}\!\left(\cos\frac{\pi l}{n+1}\right),
 \quad 1\le l\le p,
 \qquad s=\exp\!\left(\sum_{l=1}^p u_l\right).$$ There are orthonormal one-particle bases on alternate seams in which each transfer is diagonal with entries $$e^{u_1},\ldots,e^{u_p},1,e^{-u_p},\ldots,e^{-u_1}.$$ Every basis vector has site coordinates bounded by $C/\sqrt n$, for an absolute constant $C$. Moreover, $$\label{eq:mode-gap}
 u_l\ge c\frac{p+1-l}{n}$$ for an absolute $c>0$. If $t=b-a$ and $1\le k\le p$, then $$\label{eq:sector-penalty}
 \frac{\|T^{(p+k)}_{b,a}\|\,
             \|T^{(p-k)}_{b,a}\|}{s^{2t}}
 \le \exp\!\left(-c\frac{t k^2}{n}\right).$$ Finally, assign to any subset $J$ of the one-particle modes the normalized propagation weight $$w_t(J)=s^{-t}\prod_{j\in J}\sigma_j^t,$$ where the $\sigma_j$ are the displayed singular values. For every $\eta>0$, $$\label{eq:all-state-sum}
 \sum_{J\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}}w_t(J)
 =2\prod_{l=1}^p(1+e^{-t u_l})^2\le C_\eta,
 \qquad t\ge\eta n.$$ The corresponding sum for two replicas is at most $C_\eta^2$.

Fix $\eta,\rho>0$ and integer seams $0\le a\le b\le m$. If $m/n\ge\rho$, $a\ge\eta n$, and $m-b\ge\eta n$, then $$\label{eq:cap-comparison}
 \frac{\|L_a\otimes L_a\|\,
             \|R_b\otimes R_b\|\,s^{2(b-a)}}{Z_{\rm dd}}
 \le C_{\eta,\rho}.$$ In particular the bound is uniform as the two cuts vary in any fixed longitudinal interior region of a nondegenerate limiting rectangle.

Let $\mathcal T_-$ and $\mathcal T_+$ be the two-replica transfers from $a$ to $c$ and from $c$ to $b$, with column lengths $t_-$ and $t_+$. For the fixed positive widths above, so that $t_\pm\ge\eta n$ for some $\eta>0$ and all sufficiently small meshes, $$\bigl\|s^{-2(t_-+t_+)}
       \mathcal T_+\mathcal O_I\mathcal T_-\bigr\|
       \le C\left(\frac{|S(I)|}{n}\right)^2.
 \label{eq:sandwiched-insertion}$$ Consequently, uniformly over the cap-local weights $\lambda(A)\in[0,1]$, $$\frac{\bigl|\langle V_R,
       \mathcal T_+\mathcal O_I\mathcal T_-V_L\rangle\bigr|}
      {Z_{\rm dd}}
 \le C_M\left(\frac{|S(I)|}{n}\right)^2.
 \label{eq:marked-contraction-bound}$$

Let $u$ be either the horizontal or vertical coordinate, let $L=\{u=c\}$ be a test line, and let $J\subset L$ be a bounded segment. If $u$ is the vertical coordinate, assume $c>0$. Fix a bounded window $K\subset\overline{\mathbb H}$ and buffers $\rho_-,\rho_+>0$. Deterministically partition $J$ into $O(h^{-1})$ intervals of length at most $h$, with endpoints off the graph. Let $E_{\delta,h}$ be the event that, for one of these intervals $I$, one directed half-plane cycle has two portions $\alpha,\beta$ contained in $K$ such that each portion has one endpoint in $\{u\le c-\rho_-\}$ and the other in $\{u\ge c+\rho_+\}$, and $$\iota_I(\alpha)\iota_I(\beta)<0.$$ Then $$\lim_{h\downarrow0}\limsup_{\delta\downarrow0}
 \mathbb P(E_{\delta,h})=0.
 \label{eq:local-opposite-limit}$$ For a vertical line $L$, the segment may reach or extend below the bottom boundary. Test lines are chosen off lattice vertices; the same estimate holds for seam perturbations of order $\delta$.
